# Conditional execution of boolean literals

Verifies a `true` condition runs its body while a `false` condition skips it.
The skipped body contains no observable output, so only the `true` body and the
statement after both conditionals reach standard output.

>>> source
if (true) {
    print(1)
}

if (false) {
    print(2)
}

print(3)

<<< stdout
1
3

<<< stderr
